{"id":"h087","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Alan Turing's paper 'On Computable Numbers' was published in the 1930s.","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"Turing's paper was received by the Proceedings of the London Mathematical Society in May 1936.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The paper appeared in print in 1937 (Series 2, Vol. 42).","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Both the receipt date and the print date fall in the 1930s.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The standard bibliographic record gives 1936 or 1937 depending on whether receipt or print date is cited.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0},{"text":"There is essentially no substantive counterargument to the claim.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The paper is sometimes dated 1936 and sometimes 1937, which could cause confusion.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Either year, 1936 or 1937, is in the 1930s, so the claim holds under either convention.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The publication dates settle the matter, and the claim is true whichever date is used.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7